From: Baraneedharan Anbazhagan <anbazhagan@hp.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:43:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg: Fix GOP device path pool double free

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0050, as it is]

Free the previous GOP device path pool only once when the recursive
search returns a path to append. If it returns NULL, preserve paths
collected from earlier children instead of freeing the pool.

Signed-off-by: Anbazhagan Baraneedharan <anbazhagan@hp.com>

ouroBIOS backport of tianocore/edk2 commit 859d22b8ef45 (merged on
2026-11-03, after edk2-stable202608, the base of MrChromebox's
uefipayload_2608), applied unchanged. Drop it when the base includes
it.

Why here: PlatformConsole.c of PlatformBootManagerLib connects every
video controller with EfiBootManagerConnectVideoController(), which
takes the GOP device paths from EfiBootManagerGetGopDevicePath(). When
a child of the controller ended with a Controller device path node (a
GOP driver with children of its own), the old code freed the pool that
earlier children had filled twice if the search below that child found
a GOP, and returned it freed if the search found none. The boards' own
graphics (GraphicsOutputDxe on coreboot's framebuffer, an ACPI _ADR
child) never take that path; the option ROM of a graphics card in the
M920x could.

TEST=git am on the series: clean, the same lines as upstream.
---
 MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmConsole.c | 6 +-----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmConsole.c b/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmConsole.c
index 97267e0ab..d1fd2351b 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmConsole.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmConsole.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 
 Copyright (c) 2011 - 2018, Intel Corporation. All rights reserved.<BR>
 (C) Copyright 2015 Hewlett Packard Enterprise Development LP<BR>
+(c) Copyright 2026 HP Development Company, L.P.
 SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent
 
 **/
@@ -204,7 +205,6 @@ EfiBootManagerGetGopDevicePath (
           // Recursively look for GOP child in this frame buffer handle
           //
           DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "[Bds] Looking for GOP child deeper ... \n"));
-          TempDevicePath   = GopPool;
           ReturnDevicePath = EfiBootManagerGetGopDevicePath (OpenInfoBuffer[Index].ControllerHandle);
           if (ReturnDevicePath != NULL) {
             TempDevicePath = GopPool;
@@ -215,10 +215,6 @@ EfiBootManagerGetGopDevicePath (
 
             gBS->FreePool (ReturnDevicePath);
           }
-
-          if (TempDevicePath != NULL) {
-            gBS->FreePool (TempDevicePath);
-          }
         }
       }
     }
